
Defination 1:
Git Worktree is a Git feature that enables a single Git repository to have multiple working directories (called worktrees). 
Each worktree can have a different branch checked out, allowing developers to work on multiple branches simultaneously without 
cloning the repository multiple times or repeatedly stashing and switching changes.

Short Definition (Interview)

Git Worktree allows multiple working directories to share a single Git repository, enabling you to work on multiple branches at the same time without creating multiple clones.


One-Line Definition

Git Worktree is a Git feature that allows multiple branches to be checked out simultaneously in separate working directories from a single repository.


